INSERT INTO `dc_tunables` (`category`, `name`, `d3_value`, `tuned_value`, `unit`, `notes`) VALUES
('affixes', 'missile_dampening_rollable', NULL, 0.0, 'flag', 'Section B audit line 585, Architect ruling 2026-09-19: whether Missile Dampening is in the roll pool is an engine-feasibility switch of ours, not D3 pool membership. 3.3.5a has no per-projectile speed control, so it is excluded rather than left a no-op that eats a Rare pack''s one Defensive slot; set it to 1 when the engine can carry it. D3 pool membership stays sourced in elite_affix_pools.csv'),
('barbarian', 'health_potion_cooldown_seconds', 30.0, NULL, 'seconds', 'from legendary_potions.csv:d3_id=HealthPotionLegendary_01.cooldown_s, reference/d3planner/data.json /potions'),
('barbarian', 'health_potion_heal_pct', 60.0, NULL, 'percent', 'from legendary_potions.csv:d3_id=HealthPotionLegendary_01.base_heal_pct, this row''s own base_heal column: "60% of max Life", and every other row in this file says the same. Audit row 26'),
('combat', 'active_skill_slots', 6.0, NULL, 'count', 'from character_rules.csv:name=active_skill_slots.value, Diablo Wiki https://diablo.fandom.com/wiki/Elective_Mode - "allows players to freely assign any unlocked skills to any of the six action bar slots"; corroborated by https://diablo.fandom.com/wiki/Active_skill. Sourced by Gemini, docs/research/literal-audit-sources-2.md row 22'),
('combat', 'area_damage_chance', 0.2, NULL, 'multiplier', 'from damage_formula.csv:step=11. Area Damage Proc (Secondary).area_damage_chance, this row''s own formula column: "If Random(0 1) < 0.20"; 02-combat section 2. Audit row 1'),
('combat', 'area_damage_radius_yards', 10.0, NULL, 'yards', 'from damage_formula.csv:step=11. Area Damage Proc (Secondary).area_damage_radius_yards, this row''s own notes_on_buckets column: "all enemies within 10 yards". Audit rows 2, 3 and 4'),
('combat', 'big_life_hit_messages_per_second', NULL, 8.0, 'count', 'diablocraft-l9s9 (docs/contracts/big-life-messages.md): the most H records (up to 10 hits each) the server sends one player in a second. Beyond it the waiting hits fold into one sum, so the cap is a hard cap on traffic. PLACEHOLDER: the report seeds 8 (4 per second expected at 10 such hits per second); the designer sets it. Blank or 0 would send no H record, and the combat text keeps the clamped number.'),
('combat', 'big_life_pull_burst', NULL, 5.0, 'count', 'diablocraft-l9s9 (64-bit Life bead 5; report big-life-2026-10-07 section 3.4): DCBIGLIFE pull requests (the addon asks for the true max Life of a target whose UnitHealthMax is 1000000000) a player may send at once. PLACEHOLDER: the report seeds ''at most 1/s per player''; 5 lets a few quick retargets through. The designer sets it. Blank would mean the route refuses every request (docs/contracts/window-bridge.md, Budget).'),
('combat', 'big_life_pull_per_second', NULL, 1.0, 'count', 'diablocraft-l9s9 (64-bit Life bead 5; report big-life-2026-10-07 section 3.4): DCBIGLIFE pull tokens per second a player gets back. PLACEHOLDER: the report seeds ''at most 1/s per player''; the designer sets it. Blank would mean the route refuses every request (docs/contracts/window-bridge.md, Budget).'),
('combat', 'big_life_window_ms', NULL, 250.0, 'milliseconds', 'diablocraft-l9s9 (docs/contracts/big-life-messages.md): the batch window of the DCBIGLIFE pushes. A B record (a big creature''s true max Life) and an H record (a hit of 2^32 or more, exact) wait this long after the first of them is queued so a pack of creatures or a burst of hits shares messages. PLACEHOLDER: the report seeds 250 ms; the designer sets it. 0 sends on the player''s next tick.'),
('combat', 'buff_values_push_ms', NULL, 250.0, 'milliseconds', 'diablocraft-xumo (buff icons build 1): the least time between two records the server sends the addon for one buff''s values (docs/contracts/buff-values-messages.md): Gogok changes on every hit, so its Dodge line is sent at most this often, the latest value always. No D3 number and none in the brief beyond ''a few a second''. PLACEHOLDER: 250 is an engineering figure; the designer sets it. 0 sends every change.'),
('combat', 'class_buff_refresh_ms', NULL, 250.0, 'milliseconds', 'diablocraft-b3zj (buff icons build 2): how often the module looks at the conditions of the Barbarian''s passive buffs (Relentless''s Life, Berserker Rage''s Fury, Brawler''s enemy count within its radius) to put the buff on or take it off. No D3 number. PLACEHOLDER: 250 is an engineering figure; the designer sets it. A smaller step answers sooner and costs more grid searches (Brawler counts the enemies around). The Wizard''s buffs follow its own 250 ms upkeep.'),
('combat', 'dual_wield_ias_pct', 15.0, NULL, 'percent', 'from stats.csv:stat=Attack Speed.dual_wield_ias_pct, stats.csv Attack Speed how_it_stacks: ''Dual-wielding adds an additive 15% IAS into the sheet bucket''; formula_for_effect DualWield_15%'),
('combat', 'gem_aura_refresh_ms', NULL, 500.0, 'milliseconds', 'diablocraft-apkq (legendary gems 10b-4): how often the module looks at the enemies around a gem wearer and at the wearer''s own condition: Bane of the Trapped''s slow aura (refreshed this often, lasting twice as long), Pain Enhancer''s Blood Frenzy (bleeding enemies counted this often), Esoteric Alteration''s below-half-Life check and the stacks that lapse. No D3 or d3planner number (the gem texts say only that the effect follows the enemies and the Life). PLACEHOLDER: 500 is the engineering figure 10b-4 ships; the designer sets it. A smaller step answers sooner and costs more grid searches.'),
('combat', 'gem_iceblink_chill_seconds', NULL, NULL, 'seconds', 'diablocraft-y75r (legendary gems 10b-3): how long the Chill that Iceblink''s Cold skills apply lasts; the gem''s text states no duration (each Wizard rune and Barbarian rune states its own). Blank = no duration chosen, so Iceblink applies no Chill until the designer sets it.'),
('combat', 'gem_iceblink_chill_slow_pct', 60.0, NULL, 'percent', 'diablocraft-y75r (legendary gems 10b-3): the movement slow of the Chill Iceblink''s Cold skills apply, before the gem''s own additional slow. 60 is the same published figure the Wizard''s wizard_chill_slow_pct and the Barbarian chill rows use (maxroll Crowd Control Explained, adopted by ruling 2026-09-29: the current unstated D3 chill slow is 60%).'),
('combat', 'gem_mirinae_smite_range_yards', NULL, NULL, 'yards', 'diablocraft-y75r (legendary gems 10b-3): how far "a nearby enemy" is for Mirinae''s smite, measured from the player; neither the sheet nor d3planner gives a distance. Blank = no distance chosen, so the smite does not fire (the heal with it neither) until the designer sets it.'),
('combat', 'gem_moratorium_pay_period_ms', NULL, 250.0, 'milliseconds', 'diablocraft-5rv0 (return of y75r): how often Moratorium pays the damage it put off, as one combat-log line per step; a smaller step is a smoother bar and more lines. No D3 or d3planner number (the gem text says only that the damage is taken over time). PLACEHOLDER: 250 is the engineering figure y75r shipped; the designer sets it. The generator bakes it into Spell.dbc record 83404 (EffectAuraPeriod_1) and the module reads it back off that record, so changing it needs generate_spells.py and a client patch, not .dc tunables set.'),
('combat', 'gem_wreath_radius_yards', NULL, NULL, 'yards', 'diablocraft-y75r (legendary gems 10b-3): the radius of "nearby enemies" for Wreath of Lightning''s pulse, from the player; neither the sheet nor d3planner gives one. Blank = no radius chosen, so the Wreath is gained but its pulses hit nothing until the designer sets it.'),
('combat', 'ground_marker_radius_yards', NULL, 2.0, 'yards', 'diablocraft-ground-target-circles (ruling q-0930-09 "size them per skill"); the green ground cursor of a skill with no area (Teleport and its runes and Archon Teleport; Furious Charge''s target point); baked into client Spell.dbc so a change needs a client patch rebuild and release; must be a stock SpellRadius yardage (0.5 1 2 3 3.5 4 5 6 7 8 9 10 ...); worker''s starting value - the designer sets it'),
('combat', 'passive_skill_slots', 4.0, NULL, 'count', 'from character_rules.csv:name=passive_skill_slots.value, Blizzard Game Guide quoted verbatim on the official Blizzard forums https://eu.forums.blizzard.com/en/d3/t/is-there-any-way-to-get-more-than-four-passive-skills/4446 post 5 - "That''s four in total."; corroborated by Diablo Wiki https://diablo.fandom.com/wiki/Passive_skill_(Diablo_III). Sourced by Gemini, docs/research/literal-audit-sources-2.md row 23'),
('combat', 'passive_slot_1_unlock_level', 10.0, NULL, 'level', 'from character_rules.csv:name=passive_slot_1_unlock_level.value, Blizzard Game Guide quoted verbatim on the official Blizzard forums https://eu.forums.blizzard.com/en/d3/t/is-there-any-way-to-get-more-than-four-passive-skills/4446 post 5 - "As you reach levels 10, 20 and 30 (and 70 with Reaper of Souls), you''ll unlock a passive skill slot."; corroborated by Diablo Wiki https://diablo.fandom.com/wiki/Passive_skill_(Diablo_III). Sourced by Gemini, docs/research/literal-audit-sources-2.md row 18'),
('combat', 'passive_slot_2_unlock_level', 20.0, NULL, 'level', 'from character_rules.csv:name=passive_slot_2_unlock_level.value, Blizzard Game Guide quoted verbatim on the official Blizzard forums https://eu.forums.blizzard.com/en/d3/t/is-there-any-way-to-get-more-than-four-passive-skills/4446 post 5 - "As you reach levels 10, 20 and 30 (and 70 with Reaper of Souls), you''ll unlock a passive skill slot.". Sourced by Gemini, docs/research/literal-audit-sources-2.md row 19'),
('combat', 'passive_slot_3_unlock_level', 30.0, NULL, 'level', 'from character_rules.csv:name=passive_slot_3_unlock_level.value, Blizzard Game Guide quoted verbatim on the official Blizzard forums https://eu.forums.blizzard.com/en/d3/t/is-there-any-way-to-get-more-than-four-passive-skills/4446 post 5 - "As you reach levels 10, 20 and 30 (and 70 with Reaper of Souls), you''ll unlock a passive skill slot.". Sourced by Gemini, docs/research/literal-audit-sources-2.md row 20'),
('combat', 'passive_slot_4_unlock_level', 70.0, NULL, 'level', 'from character_rules.csv:name=passive_slot_4_unlock_level.value, Blizzard Game Guide quoted verbatim on the official Blizzard forums https://eu.forums.blizzard.com/en/d3/t/is-there-any-way-to-get-more-than-four-passive-skills/4446 post 5 - "As you reach levels 10, 20 and 30 (and 70 with Reaper of Souls), you''ll unlock a passive skill slot."; the fourth slot is the Reaper of Souls one. Sourced by Gemini, docs/research/literal-audit-sources-2.md row 21'),
('combat', 'passive_slot_gap_ms', NULL, 150.0, 'milliseconds', 'security.md G1 gaps; brief docs/briefs/claude-combat-g1-gaps-brief.md (ruling 2026-09-30) says start around 100-250; least time between two DCPASSIVE passive changes from one player - each waits for a database commit; 0 disables it'),
('combat', 'revive_body_limit', 3.0, NULL, 'count', 'diablocraft-uxps (docs/decisions.md 2026-10-09, the designer: D3 patch 2.0.1 rule). Most revives at the body (Revive at Corpse) in a row outside a Greater Rift before only Revive at Checkpoint or in Town are left; inside a Greater Rift there is no limit. Any revive at the checkpoint or in town starts the count again. D3 published 3: Blizzard patch 2.0.1 notes, 2014-02-25 (https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/12671560/patch-2-0-1-now-live): "Players may only resurrect at their body a maximum of three times in a row". Blank or 0 means no limit'),
('combat', 'revive_burst', NULL, 10.0, 'count', 'diablocraft-revive-choices-server: DCREVIVE (the death window: Revive here / in town / at rift start) requests a player may send at once; the same 10 the designer set for every window route (artisan_burst, jeweler_burst, q-0930-49); his to change. Blank would mean the route refuses every request (docs/contracts/window-bridge.md, Budget).'),
('combat', 'revive_per_second', NULL, 5.0, 'count', 'diablocraft-revive-choices-server: DCREVIVE tokens per second a player gets back; the same 5 the designer set for every window route (artisan_per_second, jeweler_per_second, q-0930-49); his to change. Blank would mean the route refuses every request (docs/contracts/window-bridge.md, Budget).'),
('combat', 'revive_town_spread_yards', NULL, 10.0, 'yards', 'diablocraft-uxps (docs/decisions.md 2026-10-09, the designer: town arrivals spread round the hub''s spawn, logins not included). The designer set 10 and tested it on dev 2026-10-10 (diablocraft-wt1k): radius of the disc round world_hub_points.csv spawn in which a Revive in Town (and a living player the core would send to a graveyard) lands, on dry ground the spawn can see. Blank or 0 means everyone lands on the spawn itself'),
('combat', 'skill_slot_gap_ms', NULL, 150.0, 'milliseconds', 'security.md G1 gaps; brief docs/briefs/claude-combat-g1-gaps-brief.md (ruling 2026-09-30) says start around 100-250; least time between two DCSLOT skill-bar changes from one player - each waits for a database commit; 150 is under a click-then-click on the skills screen; 0 disables it'),
('crafting', 'artisan_burst', NULL, 10.0, 'count', 'diablocraft-488x: DCARTISAN (Blacksmith and Mystic window) requests a player may send at once; ruling q-0930-49 (2026-09-30). Blank would mean the window route refuses every request (docs/contracts/window-bridge.md, Budget).'),
('crafting', 'artisan_interaction_range_yards', NULL, 5.0, 'yards', 'Codex audit 82: current artisan interaction range; no published origin found; existing literal preserved as the designer tuning.'),
('crafting', 'artisan_per_second', NULL, 5.0, 'count', 'diablocraft-488x: DCARTISAN tokens per second a player gets back; ruling q-0930-49 (2026-09-30). Blank would mean the window route refuses every request (docs/contracts/window-bridge.md, Budget).'),
('crafting', 'base_item_level', NULL, 70.0, 'level', 'Codex literal audit 114; mod-diablocraft/scripts/generate_crafting.py:155; Generated base-item template level; origin: 07-crafting R2; Template-wide display/repair input.'),
('crafting', 'blacksmith_cast_seconds', NULL, 2.0, 'seconds', 'ruling 2026-10-01: one custom two-second bar for the entire exact craft quantity.'),
('crafting', 'durability_donor_max_level', NULL, 70.0, 'level', 'Codex literal audit 117; mod-diablocraft/scripts/generate_crafting.py:156; Highest native durability donor level; origin: none found; Changes inherited repair/durability baseline.'),
('crafting', 'durability_donor_min_level', NULL, 60.0, 'level', 'Codex literal audit 116; mod-diablocraft/scripts/generate_crafting.py:156; Lowest native durability donor level; origin: none found; Changes inherited repair/durability baseline.'),
('crafting', 'gem_item_level', NULL, 70.0, 'level', 'Codex literal audit 119; mod-diablocraft/scripts/generate_crafting.py:165; Gem template item level; origin: none found; Template/display policy.'),
('crafting', 'gem_quality', NULL, 3.0, 'count', 'Codex literal audit 118; mod-diablocraft/scripts/generate_crafting.py:165; Gem item native rarity; origin: none found; Rare-quality cosmetic/template policy, not D3 gem rank.'),
('crafting', 'gem_required_level', NULL, 0.0, 'level', 'Codex literal audit 120; mod-diablocraft/scripts/generate_crafting.py:165; Gem template required character level; origin: none found; Allows use at any character level.'),
('crafting', 'gem_stack_count', NULL, 200.0, 'count', 'Codex literal audit 122; mod-diablocraft/scripts/generate_crafting.py:165; Normal gem stack limit; origin: none found; Direct bag-capacity effect.'),
('crafting', 'gm_gem_grant_max_count', NULL, 20.0, 'count', 'Codex audit 102: GM test gem-grant count cap; no published origin found; existing value preserved.'),
('crafting', 'gm_material_grant_max_count', NULL, 1000000.0, 'count', 'Codex audit 99: GM material-grant safety limit; no published origin found; existing value preserved.'),
('crafting', 'jeweler_burst', NULL, 10.0, 'count', 'diablocraft-488x: DCJEWELER (Jeweler window) requests a player may send at once; ruling q-0930-49 (2026-09-30). Blank would mean the window route refuses every request (docs/contracts/window-bridge.md, Budget).'),
('crafting', 'jeweler_per_second', NULL, 5.0, 'count', 'diablocraft-488x: DCJEWELER tokens per second a player gets back; ruling q-0930-49 (2026-09-30). Blank would mean the window route refuses every request (docs/contracts/window-bridge.md, Budget).'),
('crafting', 'repair_minimum_gold', NULL, 1.0, 'gold', 'Codex audit 98: current minimum nonzero repair price; no published origin found; the designer tuning.'),
('crafting', 'starter_feet_count', NULL, 1.0, 'count', 'Codex CSV inventory starter_kit.csv feet/count; 08-world W6 and the designer starter-kit policy; rarity remains metadata.'),
('crafting', 'starter_finger_count', NULL, 2.0, 'count', 'Codex CSV inventory starter_kit.csv finger/count; 08-world W6 and the designer starter-kit policy; rarity remains metadata.'),
('crafting', 'starter_hands_count', NULL, 1.0, 'count', 'Codex CSV inventory starter_kit.csv hands/count; 08-world W6 and the designer starter-kit policy; rarity remains metadata.'),
('crafting', 'starter_head_count', NULL, 1.0, 'count', 'Codex CSV inventory starter_kit.csv head/count; 08-world W6 and the designer starter-kit policy; rarity remains metadata.'),
('crafting', 'starter_item_level', NULL, 70.0, 'level', 'Codex literal audit 42; mod-diablocraft/src/common/dc_world.cpp:241; Starter gear roll level; origin: 08-world W6/§5; Keep aligned with start-level policy.'),
('crafting', 'starter_legs_count', NULL, 1.0, 'count', 'Codex CSV inventory starter_kit.csv legs/count; 08-world W6 and the designer starter-kit policy; rarity remains metadata.'),
('crafting', 'starter_mainhand_count', NULL, 1.0, 'count', 'Codex CSV inventory starter_kit.csv mainhand/count; 08-world W6 and the designer starter-kit policy; rarity remains metadata.'),
('crafting', 'starter_neck_count', NULL, 1.0, 'count', 'Codex CSV inventory starter_kit.csv neck/count; 08-world W6 and the designer starter-kit policy; rarity remains metadata.'),
('crafting', 'starter_offhand_count', NULL, 1.0, 'count', 'Codex CSV inventory starter_kit.csv offhand/count; 08-world W6 and the designer starter-kit policy; rarity remains metadata.'),
('crafting', 'starter_shoulders_count', NULL, 1.0, 'count', 'Codex CSV inventory starter_kit.csv shoulders/count; 08-world W6 and the designer starter-kit policy; rarity remains metadata.'),
('crafting', 'starter_torso_count', NULL, 1.0, 'count', 'Codex CSV inventory starter_kit.csv torso/count; 08-world W6 and the designer starter-kit policy; rarity remains metadata.'),
('crafting', 'starter_waist_count', NULL, 1.0, 'count', 'Codex CSV inventory starter_kit.csv waist/count; 08-world W6 and the designer starter-kit policy; rarity remains metadata.'),
('crafting', 'starter_wrists_count', NULL, 1.0, 'count', 'Codex CSV inventory starter_kit.csv wrists/count; 08-world W6 and the designer starter-kit policy; rarity remains metadata.'),
('economy', 'gem_vendor_gold', NULL, 0.0, 'gold', 'Codex literal audit 123; mod-diablocraft/scripts/generate_crafting.py:165; Gem vendor buy/sell prices; origin: none found; Both prices disabled; repeated same-line zero is one policy row.'),
('economy', 'item_sell_divisor', 25.0, NULL, 'count', 'ruling 2026-10-04 q-1004-08 (diablocraft-item-base-sell-price); a vendor pays floor(D3 ItemTable.Cost / this) for a base item (data/d3/base_item_costs.csv); d3_value 25 is D3''s own: Inventory.SellItem pays Math.Floor(item.GetPrice() / 25f), blizzless-diiis 6292f950aed3b29c58f35ce55caff6fd6c9d16b5 src/DiIiS-NA/D3-GameServer/GSSystem/PlayerSystem/Inventory.cs:327-337 (docs/research/item-sell-prices.md 2.2); value blank = D3''s; a change needs generate_sql.py rerun and its items_0021_item_sell_price.sql applied, a .dc tunables set does not move SellPrice.'),
('economy', 'legacy_gold_bar_stack_count', NULL, 2147483647.0, 'count', 'Codex literal audit 112; mod-diablocraft/scripts/generate_crafting.py:147; Legacy Gold Bar maximum stack; origin: none found; Chosen inventory stack size equals signed-int ceiling; legacy denomination is retired.'),
('economy', 'legendary_gem_sell_gold', NULL, 16.0, 'gold', 'the designer, card q-1006-04 (docs/decisions.md 2026-10-06, diablocraft-ozl9): the price a vendor pays for any legendary gem item, written to SellPrice as it is (this project''s gold is the core''s money unit, dc_economy.h CopperPerGold 1, as gem_vendor_gold is). The buy price stays gem_vendor_gold (0): no vendor sells them. Regenerate generate_legendary_gem_items.py and apply its world migration'),
('economy', 'starter_satchel_count', NULL, 2.0, 'count', 'Codex literal audit 36; mod-diablocraft/src/common/dc_world.cpp:38; Satchels granted to each character; origin: comment above GrantStarterBags; Also sets existing-character top-up target.'),
('economy', 'stash_launch_tabs', NULL, 1.0, 'count', 'audit row 31 LaunchTabs; decisions.md 2026-09-10 "one tab free and four more purchasable"'),
('economy', 'stash_max_tabs', NULL, 5.0, 'count', 'audit row 30 MaxTabs; decisions.md 2026-09-10, quoted in dc_stash.h''s header comment. Ours: D3 sells more than five'),
('economy', 'stash_tab_2_price_gold', NULL, 100000.0, 'gold', 'ruling 2026-10-04 q-1004-05 (q-1003-30); tab 2 price; regenerate generate_account_economy.py and apply its stash migration.'),
('economy', 'stash_tab_3_price_gold', NULL, 100000.0, 'gold', 'ruling 2026-10-04 q-1004-05 (q-1003-30); tab 3 price; regenerate generate_account_economy.py and apply its stash migration.'),
('economy', 'stash_tab_4_price_gold', NULL, 100000.0, 'gold', 'ruling 2026-10-04 q-1004-05 (q-1003-30); tab 4 price; regenerate generate_account_economy.py and apply its stash migration.'),
('economy', 'stash_tab_5_price_gold', NULL, 100000.0, 'gold', 'ruling 2026-10-04 q-1004-05 (q-1003-30); tab 5 price; regenerate generate_account_economy.py and apply its stash migration.'),
('economy', 'tester_coffer_gems', NULL, 20.0, 'count', 'the designer-approved docs/briefs/codex-tester-coffer-brief.md 2026-09-23; target per Flawless Royal colour.'),
('economy', 'tester_coffer_gold', NULL, 500000000000.0, 'gold', 'the designer-approved docs/briefs/codex-tester-coffer-brief.md 2026-09-23; account gold target; Torment dc_economy.h CopperPerGold is 1.'),
('economy', 'tester_coffer_materials', NULL, 100000.0, 'count', 'the designer-approved docs/briefs/codex-tester-coffer-brief.md 2026-09-23; target per tracked account material.'),
('economy', 'tester_coffer_paragon', NULL, 200.0, 'level', 'the designer-approved docs/briefs/codex-tester-coffer-brief.md 2026-09-23; target for the active Paragon pool.'),
('economy', 'wing_shirt_vendor_gold', NULL, 0.0, 'gold', 'Codex literal audit 229; mod-diablocraft/scripts/generate_wings.py:263; Wing shirt vendor buy/sell prices; origin: generated SQL comment: tunables, cosmetic shirts/no prices/level 1/bind on pickup; Columns BuyPrice and SellPrice are zero.'),
('loot', 'ancient_chance_pct', 10.0, NULL, 'percent', 'diablocraft-t3t8 (ruling 2026-10-10, docs/decisions.md). The chance that a Legendary or Set drop is Ancient, from the ancient_min_tier up and at ancient_min_item_level or more, from every source (kills, chests, Kadala, the first-kill legendary, the set cache). D3: kadala.csv ancient_chance_at_level_70 (10%), drop_rates.csv ancient_primal (roughly 10% at Torment X)'),
('loot', 'ancient_min_item_level', 70.0, NULL, 'level', 'diablocraft-t3t8. The lowest item level (the monster''s level at the drop, the character''s level for a gamble) that can drop an Ancient or Primal. D3: drop_rates.csv ancient_primal, kadala.csv ancient_chance_at_level_70 (level 70)'),
('loot', 'ancient_min_tier', 5.0, NULL, 'count', 'diablocraft-t3t8. The lowest difficulty tier id that can drop an Ancient or Primal: 5 is Torment I (dc_tier_phase: Normal 1, Hard 2, Expert 3, Master 4, Torment I 5). D3: drop_rates.csv ancient_primal (level 70 Legendary or Set items on Torment I and above)'),
('loot', 'aoe_range_yards', NULL, 30.0, 'yards', 'Area looting range: your own drops on every corpse of yours within this many yards of you show in one window. The designer, q-0930-59 (option 1, 30 yards); docs/proposals/corpse-loot-minimum.md M6. The code clamps it to 5-100'),
('loot', 'blood_shard_cap_base', 500.0, NULL, 'count', 'diablocraft-gw9h; docs/proposals/kadala.md 4.2 (ruling q-1007-08). The most Blood Shards an account holds in one mode before any Greater Rift is beaten alone. D3: kadala.csv blood_shard_capacity_base (500)'),
('loot', 'blood_shard_cap_per_gr_level', 10.0, NULL, 'count', 'diablocraft-gw9h; docs/proposals/kadala.md 4.2 (ruling q-1007-08). Blood Shards added to the cap for each Greater Rift level the account has beaten alone in time in that mode, its best, kept when the character is deleted. D3: kadala.csv blood_shard_capacity_increase_per_gr (+10)'),
('loot', 'full_roll_primary_affixes', 4.0, NULL, 'count', 'from rarity_tiers.csv:rarity=Rare.primary_affix_max, rarity_tiers.csv Rare primary_affixes ''up to 4'' and secondary_affixes ''up to 2'' (max 4 primary + 2 secondary)'),
('loot', 'full_roll_secondary_affixes', 2.0, NULL, 'count', 'from rarity_tiers.csv:rarity=Rare.secondary_affix_max, rarity_tiers.csv Rare primary_affixes ''up to 4'' and secondary_affixes ''up to 2'' (max 4 primary + 2 secondary)'),
('loot', 'kadala_legendary_pct', 10.0, NULL, 'percent', 'diablocraft-aeo7; docs/proposals/kadala.md 4.7 (ruling q-1007-08). The flat chance that a Kadala gamble is a legendary or set item, not raised by Magic Find or the tier. D3: kadala.csv legendary_gamble_chance (10%). A legendary roll with no unique base for the slot, class and level falls back to the rare roll'),
('loot', 'loot_buffer_seconds', NULL, 60.0, 'seconds', 'audit row 43 BufferSeconds; how long a rolled drop is held for delivery. Code comment "L5", 06-loot L5. Ours, no D3 counterpart'),
('loot', 'magic_find_legendary_efficiency_pct', 10.0, NULL, 'percent', 'from drop_rates.csv:section=magic_find|topic=item-based Magic Find (Cain''s Fate set, Nagelring only in 2.7.x).magic_find_legendary_efficiency_pct, this row''s own value column: "10% efficiency vs Legendaries". Audit row 52'),
('loot', 'magic_find_magic_efficiency_pct', 100.0, NULL, 'percent', 'from drop_rates.csv:section=magic_find|topic=item-based Magic Find (Cain''s Fate set, Nagelring only in 2.7.x).magic_find_magic_efficiency_pct, stats.csv:21 formula_for_effect, "+100% to Magic items" - sourced by Gemini, docs/research/literal-audit-sources-2.md row 54, confirming what dc_loot.h had inferred. Not stated on this row, which gives only the Rare and Legendary penalties. Audit row 54'),
('loot', 'magic_find_rare_efficiency_pct', 30.0, NULL, 'percent', 'from drop_rates.csv:section=magic_find|topic=item-based Magic Find (Cain''s Fate set, Nagelring only in 2.7.x).magic_find_rare_efficiency_pct, this row''s own value column: "30% efficiency vs Rares". Audit row 53'),
('loot', 'magic_primary_affixes', NULL, 1.0, 'count', 'diablocraft-geyf (GitHub #58). Primary affixes rolled on a Magic item. NOT a D3 number: rarity_tiers.csv says Magic has 1-2 affixes in total and the primary/secondary split is NOT PUBLISHED. 1 is the value CountsFor had compiled in (05-items I8 implementation pick, ours), moved here unchanged'),
('loot', 'magic_secondary_affixes', NULL, 1.0, 'count', 'diablocraft-geyf (GitHub #58). Secondary affixes rolled on a Magic item. NOT a D3 number: rarity_tiers.csv gives 1-2 in total, split NOT PUBLISHED. 1 is the value CountsFor had compiled in (05-items I8 implementation pick, ours), moved here unchanged'),
('loot', 'primal_chance_pct', 0.2, 0.25, 'percent', 'diablocraft-t3t8 (ruling 2026-10-10: about 0.25%, 1 in 400). The chance that a Legendary or Set drop is Primal Ancient once the account has unlocked Primals (primal_unlock_solo_gr); it takes the first slice of the roll, so the Ancient chance above is unchanged. D3: kadala.csv primal_ancient_chance (about 0.2%, 1 in 400 to 1 in 500)'),
('loot', 'primal_unlock_solo_gr', 70.0, NULL, 'level', 'diablocraft-t3t8. The solo Greater Rift level the ACCOUNT must have beaten, in the character''s mode (normal or hardcore), before a Primal Ancient can drop. D3 unlocks it once per game mode for the whole account: drop_rates.csv ancient_primal ''Primal chance'' (unlocked after solo Greater Rift 70, once per game mode), kadala.csv primal_ancient_chance (requires unlocking solo GR70 on the account). Read from dc_account_gr_solo'),
('loot', 'rift_legendary_bonus_base_pct', 25.0, NULL, 'percent', 'from drop_rates.csv:section=base_drop_by_source|topic=rift guardian (Nephalem Rift).rift_legendary_bonus_base_pct, this row''s own details column: "bonus starts at 25% (base difficulty)". Audit row 50'),
('loot', 'rift_legendary_bonus_torment_one_pct', 44.0, NULL, 'percent', 'from drop_rates.csv:section=base_drop_by_source|topic=rift guardian (Nephalem Rift).rift_legendary_bonus_torment_one_pct, this row''s own details column: "44% at Torment I". Audit row 51. Torment II upward is deliberately absent: it is not published (dc_loot.h comment L2)'),
('loot', 'smart_loot_off_class_pct', 15.0, NULL, 'percent', 'from drop_rates.csv:section=smart_loot|topic=off-class drop chance.off_class_pct, this row''s own value column: "15% of items drop with stats for a random class other than the current one". Audit row 45; the code''s 0.85 is 1 - this'),
